uding wrapped headings and Workout feedback.\n- Background workout controls are unavailable during the modal while the existing appropriate functional clocks/rest continue; close/reopen retains drafts and keyboard dismissal/focus return.\n\nDesign evidence: `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/CURRENT-REQUIREMENTS-AUTHORITY.md`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/consolidated-fallback/INDIVIDUAL-CORRECTION-REGISTER-2026-11-03.md`, `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/VISUAL-CONTRACTS.md`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/scene.html`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/review-cases.json`\n\n### REQ-017 — Readable movement groups and label/control rhythm\n\nReadable movement groups and label/control rhythm. Shared owner: Shared form grouping / ChoiceGroup / Effort / movement lists. Current cross-checks C05, C42, C47; full notes R108, R109, R111, R112, R131.\n\n- C05 — Keep complete movement groups together and slightly increase the gap between groups.\n- C42 — Comfortable choice-label gaps matching fields; retain the good rounds-heading gap and separate dynamic count.\n- C47 — Remove the exact added tick-each-movement/blank-is-not-recorded paragraph; preserve the underlying semantics.\n- Match selection-label spacing to the accepted field rhythm; keep the good Rounds completed heading gap and add breathing room before the completion-count label.\n- Increase space between complete movement-entry groups, not between fields belonging to the same movement; retain identity, measurements and effort together.\n- Remove the exact Tick each movement you performed / blank field saved as not recorded helper paragraph without replacing it with new instructional prose or changing performed/unrecorded semantics.\n\nDesign evidence: `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/CURRENT-REQUIREMENTS-AUTHORITY.md`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/consolidated-fallback/INDIVIDUAL-CORRECTION-REGISTER-2026-11-03.md`, `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/VISUAL-CONTRACTS.md`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/V10-superset.png`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/scene.html`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/review-cases.json`\n\n### REQ-018 — Contained scrolling without a lower gap, opening outline or scrollbar\n\nContained scrolling without a lower gap, opening outline or scrollbar. Shared owner: LoggingOverlay native frame / typography wrapper / inner scroll region. Current cross-checks C44, C57, C58, C59; full notes R16, R128, R129, R140. Visual/acceptance references: P01, P02, P03.\n\n- C44 — Stationary continuous frame/surface; inner scroll; Notes/Save reachable through long/narrow/keyboard cases.\n- C57 — Delegated final polish R140/R145: visible scrolling control edges meet the inner lower dialog border; retain stationary outer frame and chamfer.\n- C58 — Delegated final polish R140/R145: no unwanted automatic blue container outline on first load/open/reopen, especially mobile; retain modal focus and intentional keyboard focus on controls.\n- C59 — Delegated final polish R140/R145: hide all scrollbar chrome, including ghost overlays; preserve touch/wheel/keyboard scrolling and Notes/Save access.\n- P01: clipped vertical control strokes extend to the inner lower frame boundary without the blank inset strip; preserve intended chamfer clipping and do not restore an interior line crossing Reps/Effort/Notes.\n- P02: no automatic blue outline surrounds the whole inner form/scroll container on first load/open/reopen, especially mobile; diagnose the actual focus/outline owner and retain modal focus and intentional keyboard focus on controls.\n- P03: hide all scrollbar chrome including translucent overlays while wheel/touch/keyboard and focus scrolling still work, with no horizontal overflow or unreachable Notes/Save.\n- Use available viewport/safe-area/keyboard space rather than the rejected arbitrary half-height cap; ordinary short forms avoid unnecessary scroll and genuinely long forms remain internally scrollable.\n\nDesign evidence: `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/CURRENT-REQUIREMENTS-AUTHORITY.md`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/consolidated-fallback/INDIVIDUAL-CORRECTION-REGISTER-2026-11-03.md`, `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/VISUAL-CONTRACTS.md`, `sources/source-01-source-01-current-authority/FINAL-POLISH-ACCEPTANCE.md`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/scene.html`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/review-cases.json`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/P01-acceptance-schematic.svg`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/P02-acceptance-schematic.svg`, `sources/source-02-source-02-supporting-evidence/visuals/P03-acceptance-schematic.svg`\n\n\n## Evidence coverage\n\n- EVID-F1CA58C8F8CF — G20: Dedicated platform copy/terminology/tone pass. Visible labels say Effort, preserving historical values/meaning. Apply explicit removals and Log when complete wording. Remove annotated EMOM Not started/Work captions, retaining minute progress/Now/Next.\n- EVID-7D8A182C812B — C05: Multi-movement rhythm\n- EVID-89C9B0E829A2 — G01: Common movement hierarchy: prominent name, prescription/load, quiet equipment, aligned action slot; separators between peers, no inner vertical rail/final-item rule. Remove the added Last-performance row. On cards with multiple movements, slightly increase spacing between complete movement groups while keeping each group coherent (R111).\n- EVID-CA60B690316D — C40: Logging title hierarchy\n- EVID-322226CF903F — C41: Dialog header\n- EVID-973155BD82DF — C42: Label/control spacing\n- EVID-C5975EB7BB4B — C43: Dialog backdrop\n- EVID-4DF2155092D3 — C44: Dialog scrolling\n- EVID-876928C79721 — C47: Superset helper removal\n- EVID-5